An example from a rehab project we have been working on for a while.

The project receives strong support from informational queries, while also improving visibility for commercial terms. In May 2026, it was able to benefit positively from the BCAU in a clear way.

Most of the time, topical authority comes from two main paths:

1. Entity-first topical authority
    You take one main entity, such as “addiction,” and process all of its attributes, types, causes, symptoms, treatments, risks, and related concepts.
2. Query-template topical authority
    You take a query template and process all of its variations by covering every entity that shares the same relation.

In this case, informational queries help us rank better for location-specific commercial terms as well.

AI citations from informational prompts also support rankings for “location + service” query templates, because the search engine and AI systems start associating the brand with the broader topical context, not only the direct commercial pages.

This is why informational SEO is not separate from commercial SEO.

It builds the source context, strengthens topical authority, and improves the probability of being selected for commercial queries.

